#heading(level: 2, numbering: none)[Appendix] <app:local-residues>

#subsection[Residues with respect to sections of vector bundles]
<ss:section-residues>
Let $X$ be a complex analytic manifold of dimension $n$. It is known that to
each divisor $D$ on $X$ with locally defined functions
$f_alpha in scr(O) (scr(U)_alpha)$ there corresponds a linear bundle $L = [D]$
with transition functions ${g_(alpha beta) = f_alpha \/ f_beta}$. The local
residue $res_a omega$ of the form $omega$ with polar divisor
$F_1 + dots.c + F_n$ at a point $a in Z = F_1 inter dots.c inter F_n$ (see
@ss:divisors) can be treated as a residue with respect to the holomorphic
section $f = f_1 (z) e_1 + dots.c + f_n (z) e_n$ of the vector bundle
$E = [F_1] plus.o dots.c plus.o [F_n]$, where ${e_k}$ is the frame of the
bundle, and $z$ are local coordinates. We can actually define a local residue
with respect to a holomorphic section with an isolated zero in an arbitrary
vector bundle $E -> X$ of rank $n$. Consider the vector space of sections
$H^0 (X, scr(O) (K times.o det E))$, where $K = and.big^n T_X^(*')$ is the
highest exterior power of the holomorphic cotangent bundle. An element of this
space in terms of the local holomorphic frame ${e_k}$ on $E$ and the local
holomorphic coordinates $z$ on $X$ has the form
$psi = h(z) (d z_1 and dots.c and d z_n) times.o (e_1 and dots.c and e_n)$. With
the element $psi$ and the section $f = f_1 (z) e_1 + dots.c + f_n (z) e_n$ we
associate the differential form
$
  psi/f = frac(h(z) d z_1 and dots.c and d z_n, f_1 (z) dots.c f_n (z)).
$ <eq:section-form>
On the assumption that the section $f$ has an isolated zero at the point
$a in X$ we define the residue
$
  res_a (psi \/ f) = res_a ""_f (h)
$ <eq:section-residue>
#source(71)as the local residue of the form @eq:section-form at the point $a$.
Although the right-hand side of @eq:section-form depends on the choice of frame
and coordinates, the transformation formula (see @ss:transformation-formula) and
the rule for transforming an integral by changing the coordinates show that the
residue @eq:section-residue does not depend on this choice. The following
theorem on the total sum of residues is true (see @bib:Griffiths1978b,
@bib:Griffiths1978a[p.~731]): _if $E -> X$ is a holomorphic vector bundle of
rank $n$ over a compact complex analytic manifold $X$ of dimension $n$, and
$f in H^0 (X, scr(O) (E))$ is a holomorphic section with discrete set of zeros
$Z$, then for any element $psi in H^0 (X, scr(O) (K times.o det E))$_
$
  sum_(a in Z) res_a (psi/f) = 0.
$
#new-par
About the converse of this theorem, see @bib:Griffiths1978b.

#subsection[Residues with respect to vector fields and the Bott formula]
<ss:vector-field-residues>
We consider separately residues with respect to sections of a holomorphic
tangent bundle, that is, residues with respect to holomorphic vector fields. Let
$X$ be a compact complex analytic manifold of dimension $n$, let $T'$ be a
holomorphic tangent bundle for $X$, and let $L$ be a linear holomorphic bundle
over $X$. We denote by $scr(L)$ the sheaf of germs of holomorphic sections of
the bundle $L$. We are interested in the bundle $E = T' times.o L$ of rank $n$.
With the section $V in H^0 (X, T' times.o L)$ we associate the linear
convolution operator
$
  i(V): Omega^p -> Omega^(p - 1) times.o scr(L)
$
(here $Omega^p$ is the sheaf of germs of holomorphic $p$-forms on $X$), which in
the local coordinates $z$ is defined as follows. If
$V = sum f_i partial \/ partial z_i$, where $f_i$ are local sections of the
sheaf $scr(L)$, then $i(V) (d z_i) = f_i$; in the general case
$
  i(V) (g(z) d z_I) = sum_k (-1)^(k - 1) f_(i_k) g d z_(I without {i_k}).
$
Thus, in the sheaf of rings $Omega^0 = scr(O)$ we can define the sheaf of ideals
$I = i(V) (Omega^1 times.o scr(L)^(-1))$: at each point $a in X$ the fiber of
this sheaf is the ideal $I_a subset scr(O)_a$ generated by the family of germs
${f_j times.o scr(L)^(-1), j = 1, ..., n}$. We denote the set of zeros of the
sheaf of ideals $I$ by $Z$; it coincides with the zero set of the section $V$.
The element $psi in H^0 (scr(U), scr(O) (K times.o det(T' times.o L)))$ in a
neighborhood $scr(U) subset X$ has the form
$h(z) (d z_1 and dots.c and d z_n) times.o
(partial \/ partial z_1 and dots.c and partial \/ partial z_n)$ with local
coordinates $z$, where $h$ is the section of $scr(L)^n$ over $scr(U)$. As in
@ss:section-residues[subsection], we have defined the local residues
$
  res_a (psi/V) = res_a ""_V (h)
$ <eq:field-residue>
with respect to the vector field $V$. Thus, for the set $h = {h_a}_(a in Z)$ of
germs $h_a in scr(L)_a^n$ we can construct the global residue
$
  Res_V (h) = sum_(a in Z) res_a ""_V (h).
$
#source(72)Let us introduce the notation
$scr(L)_Z^n = scr(L)^n times.o (scr(O) \/ I)$. Then, taking account of the
proposition in @ss:integral-definition, we have defined a mapping
$Res: H^0 (X, scr(L)_Z^n) -> CC$ that has the following property (see
@bib:Carrell1978): _if $Z$ is a finite nonempty set, then there is a mapping
$m: H^0 (X, scr(L)_Z^n) -> H^n (X, Omega^n)$ (depending only on $V$) such that
the diagram_
$
  #cd(
    node((0, 0), $H^0 (X, scr(L)_Z^n)$),
    node((1, 0), $CC$),
    node((0, 1), $H^n (X, Omega^n)$),
    edge((0, 0), (1, 0), $Res$, "->", label-side: left),
    edge((0, 0), (0, 1), $(-1)^n m$, "->", label-side: right),
    edge((0, 1), (1, 0), $tr$, "->", label-side: right),
  )
$ <eq:residue-diagram>
_is commutative, where the trace $tr phi$ is equal to the integral
$(2 pi i)^(-n) integral_X eta(phi)$ of the form $eta(phi)$ corresponding to the
element $phi$ under the Dolbeault isomorphism
$H^n (X, Omega^n) limits(tilde.eq)^eta H_(dbar)^(n, n) (X) tilde.eq H^(2n) (X)$
(here the last group is the de Rham cohomology group)._

Thus, integration over the compact complex manifold $X$ reduces to the
calculation of the total sum of the local residues at the zeros of holomorphic
vector fields.

Consider the case when $L$ is a trivial bundle. If $V$ is a global vector field
on $X$, then its expansion with respect to the natural frame
${partial \/ partial z_j}$ has the property that at each zero $a$ of the field
$V$ the matrices $A_a = (partial f_i \/ partial z_j)_a$ and
$A'_a = (partial f_i \/ partial w_j)_a$ of the linear parts of $V$ in the local
coordinates $z$ and $w$ are conjugate (here we assume that
$V = sum f_i partial \/ partial z_i$). Therefore for any invariant polynomial
$P$ (see @bib:Griffiths1978a[p.~403]) the numbers $P(A_a)$ depend only on $V$
and the points $a in Z = {V = 0}$. These numbers are the values at points $a$ of
the germs of holomorphic functions $h_a (z) = P(A_z)$, where
$A_z = (partial f_i \/ partial z_j)$. Since the diagram @eq:residue-diagram is
commutative, the global residue $Res_V (h)$ of the set of germs
$h = {h_a}_(a in Z)$ is expressed in terms of the integral over the manifold
$X$. If the degree of the polynomial $P$ is equal to $n$, then, as calculation
shows, to the element $m(h)$ there corresponds under the Dolbeault isomorphism
the $(n, n)$-form $P(Theta)$, where $Theta$ is the curvature matrix of the
tangent bundle $T'$. As a result we obtain the following #index-mark(
  "Formula",
  sub: "Bott",
)_Bott formula_ @bib:Bott1967a, @bib:Bott1967b:
$
  sum_(a in Z) res_a ""_V (h) = (-2 pi i)^(-n) integral_X P(Theta).
$ <eq:bott-formula>
In the case when all of the zeros of the field $V$ are simple, the local
residues on the left-hand side are easily calculated, and we obtain
$
  sum_(V(a) = 0) frac(P(A_a), det A_a) = (-2 pi i)^(-n) integral_X P(Theta).
$
#new-par
For various aspects of formulas of the form @eq:bott-formula that have to do
with characteristic numbers of bundles and zeros of meromorphic vector fields,
see the papers of Baum and Bott @bib:Baum1970, Carrell @bib:Carrell1978, and
Toledo @bib:Toledo1973, the paper of Toledo and Tong @bib:Toledo1975 is devoted
to holomorphic variants of the Lefschetz #source(73) fixed point formula (see
also @bib:Toledo1973, @bib:Tong1973). Ohtsuki's paper @bib:Ohtsuki1982 gives a
residue formula for Chern classes associated with logarithmic connections.
